        {
            "id": "91a7ec3a-6a11-4775-b161-8ff8229b01f0",
            "build_id": "1dbab1be-68da-439d-8473-bf257477664b",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-25T19:11:56.717079+00:00",
            "notes": "Probably the most important round for this build -  [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) is the GOAT, and if you played somewhat well in the last 2 rounds, you should be easily able to afford it, together with a few greens, or a blue.\n\nWith the purchase comes a change in the playstyle as well - Deadeye becomes obsolute, and you should **NOT** use it in 99% of situations. It's simply not worth handicapping yourself just to *maybe* kill something after standing still for a few seconds. Power creep is high in Stadium, and that includes mobility and survivability, so even though the ult is *okay* in standard play, it is nearly bait to use it here.\n\nFurthermore, you will now populate the enemy flank permanently. You of course shouldn't push all the way to the enemy spawn, and you should try to stay somewhat close to your team in case a duel goes wrong or the whole enemy team rushes you, especially if you have e.g.  [Kiriko](hero_70a0ac5c-2a55-4fab-beeb-2f570886426f) on your team.\n\nMake smart decisions around timing of your flanks and your positioning, and you will be two-tapping the whole enemy backline out of existence. \n\n**POWER:**\n\n [Bullseye](item_19cf3c95-5071-425e-beba-30af6ba15ef1) - 2s reduction on Combat Roll for each headshot is just nuts. If you live on the flank from this round onwards (as you should), you should be able to fit in a headshot or two before the enemy team catches on to you, and Roll should be back by that point thanks to Bullseye. Weave in, weave out.\n\n**CORE ITEMS:**\n\n- \u2b50 [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) - as I stated before, the GOAT. Never sell it, and try to get your ult as quickly as possible in the start of each round.\n- \u2b50 [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) - keep it, more damage.\n- \u2b50 [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) - keep it, more damage.\n\n**OPTIONAL:**",
